The sum of the interior angles of a convex pentagon is $(5-2) \times 180^\circ = 3 \times 180^\circ = 540^\circ$. Thus, we have
\begin{align*} (x+1) + 2x + 3x + 4x + (5x-1) &= 540 \\ x+1 + 2x + 3x + 4x + 5x - 1 &= 540 \\ (1+2+3+4+5)x + (1-1) &= 540 \\ 15x &= 540 \\ x &= \frac{540}{15} \\ x &= 36 \end{align*}
The angles are:
\begin{align*} x+1 &= 36+1 = 37^\circ \\ 2x &= 2(36) = 72^\circ \\ 3x &= 3(36) = 108^\circ \\ 4x &= 4(36) = 144^\circ \\ 5x-1 &= 5(36)-1 = 180-1 = 179^\circ \end{align*}
